<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>You & Me 🩷</title>

<style>
body {
  background: #fff5f8;
  font-family: "Comic Sans MS", cursive;
  text-align: center;
  color: #6b3b52;
  padding: 30px;
}

h1, h2 {
  color: #d65c91;
}

.card {
  background: white;
  max-width: 650px;
  margin: 25px auto;
  padding: 30px;
  border-radius: 25px;
  box-shadow: 0 5px 20px #ffd1e3;
  line-height: 1.7;
}

.puppy {
  font-size: 90px;
  cursor: pointer;
  animation: bounce 2s infinite;
}

@keyframes bounce {
  50% {
    transform: translateY(-10px);
  }
}

.reason {
  display: none;
  font-size: 22px;
  color: #d65c91;
  margin-top: 20px;
}

button {
  background: #ffc7df;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 20px;
  padding: 15px 25px;
  font-size: 18px;
  font-family: inherit;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.petal {
  position: fixed;
  top: -20px;
  animation: fall 6s linear infinite;
  font-size: 25px;
}

@keyframes fall {
  from {
    transform: translateY(-20px);
  }
  to {
    transform: translateY(110vh);
  }
}
</style>

<script>
let reasons = [
  "💗 I love how gentle u are with me.",
  "💗 I love how safe u make me feel.",
  "💗 I love ur gorgeous eyes.",
  "💗 I love you."
];

let number = 0;

function showReason() {
  document.getElementById("reason").style.display = "block";
  document.getElementById("reason").innerHTML = reasons[number];
  number++;

  if (number >= reasons.length) {
    number = 0;
  }
}
</script>

</head>

<body>

<h1>🌸 Hi my love 🥹</h1>

<div class="card">

<div class="puppy" onclick="showReason()">🐶</div>

<p>
I tried making u something else too
</p>

<p>
I hope u enjoy cutie
</p>

<div id="reason" class="reason"></div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🌱 How it started</h2>

<p>
The day I met u on MM2 was the best day of my life.
</p>

<p>
I’m so glad we talked about our cats.
I never knew that one conversation would become something
so special.
</p>

<p>
Eventually, we fell in love with each other.
</p>

<p>
I’m so grateful that I met u. 💗
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🌸 Things I love about you (everything) </h2>

<p>
There are so many things I love about you.
</p>

<p>
🌸 Your kindness
<br>
🌸 Your generosity
<br>
🌸 Your sweet heart
<br>
🌸 Your little giggle that makes me smile
<br>
🌸 The way you make me feel loved and cared for
</p>

<p>
I love every part of you, my sweet boy. 🐶💕
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>✈️ Our lil future </h2>

<p>
One day, we’re going to visit Japan together. 🌸
</p>

<p>
We’ll explore everything, buy 100 figures and mangas ,
try out the food, learn the culture, and vidit all the places we’ve dreamed of seeing.
</p>

<p>
I can’t wait to make those memories with u,
watch u achieve ur dream goals,
and travel the world with u, my love. 💗
</p>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>🐶 A little reminder</h2>

<p>
Click the puppy whenever you need a reminder of how loved you are. 🌸
</p>

</div>


<div class="petal">🌸</div>
<div class="petal" style="left:25%;animation-delay:2s;">🌸</div>
<div class="petal" style="left:50%;animation-delay:4s;">🌸</div>
<div class="petal" style="left:80%;animation-delay:1s;">🌸</div>

</body>
</html>
<script>

let reasons = [
"💗 I love how gentle u are with me.",
"💗 I love how safe u make me feel.",
"💗 I love ur gorgeous eyes.",
"💗 I love you."
];

let number = 0;

function showReason() {
  document.getElementById("reason").innerHTML = reasons[number];
  document.getElementById("reason").style.display = "block";

  number++;

  if (number >= reasons.length) {
    number = 0;
  }
}

</script>
